WEBVTT

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:31.302
which may explain a lot
of your own experience,

00:05:31.326 --> 00:05:34.613
especially if my mock interview
with Dave Chang at the top of the show

00:05:34.637 --> 00:05:36.182
sounded familiar.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.080
The failings of job interviews
hurt all of us.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:41.166
Whether we're the ones
asking the questions,

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.727
or answering them.

00:05:43.163 --> 00:05:45.334
I want to explore how we can improve them.

00:05:45.358 --> 00:05:48.293
Not just to help interviewers
make better hiring decisions,

00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:52.110
but to give job candidates a better chance
to showcase their strengths.

00:05:53.431 --> 00:05:56.519
Look, I know many companies
aren't hiring right now,

00:05:56.543 --> 00:05:58.337
but on the other side of this crisis,

00:05:58.361 --> 00:06:00.482
I hope there will be many
new job openings.